Z||000000||lews84||10-17-1999||10:51 PM||||After a short drive in my 84 SE the left alloy wheels were slightly warm. The right wheels were so hot I could barely touch them.<BR>Are both right calipers seized?<P>I have already had the left front caliper replaced. If I am replacing the 2 right calipers should I just bite the bullet and replace the left rear while I am at it?<P>Forget the question about braided steel brake lines. I found an archive on the subject and this car is not going to be raced so forget it.<P>[This message has been edited by lews84 (edited 10-17-1999).]<p>[This message has been edited by lews84 (edited 10-18-1999).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||10-17-1999||11:02 PM||||On the brake lines bit, I'd say if your stock lines are in good shape just leave 'em be.  Steel braided run a fair amount of money.  You will notice a difference in braking though.  Unless you have air in your lines, you will have next to no "squishyness" in the pedal, but you will not notice much else with them.  If you do get some, make sure they're DOT approved.||||reg||1
